{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"languages":["swift"]}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo"]]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo\/color"},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"symbolKind":"property","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLColor","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"color","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL10MXLTremoloV5colorAA8MXLColorVSgvp","roleHeading":"Instance Property","role":"symbol"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element."}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltremolo\/color"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTremolo":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"The tremolo ornament can be used to indicate single-note, double-note, or unmeasured tremolos. Single-note","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"tremolos use the single type, double-note tremolos use the start and stop types, and unmeasured tremolos use","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the unmeasured type. The default is “single” for compatibility with Version 1.1. The text of the element","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"indicates the number of tremolo marks and is an integer from 0 to 8. Note that the number of attached beams is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not included in this value, but is represented separately using the beam element. The value should be 0 for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"unmeasured tremolos.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltremolo","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTremolo"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLTremolo","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLTremolo"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLColor":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The color type indicates the color of an element. Color may be represented as hexadecimal RGB triples, as in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"HTML, or as hexadecimal ARGB tuples, with the A indicating alpha of transparency. An alpha value of 00 is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"totally transparent; FF is totally opaque. If RGB is used, the A value is assumed to be FF."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlcolor","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLColor","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLColor"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLColor","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLTremolo/color":{"kind":"symbol","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLTremolo\/color","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"color"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL8MXLColorV","text":"MXLColor"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"title":"color","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxltremolo\/color","abstract":[{"text":"The color attribute group indicates the color of an element.","type":"text"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"}}}